在美国的中小学里？

510
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:49,120
And what can be done to get more widespread adoption
那么，我们能做些什么来推动它更广泛地被采纳？

511
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,940
of civics education in school?
在学校中普及公民教育？

512
00:25:50,940 --> 00:25:52,040
So Nick, why?
所以尼克，为什么？

513
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:55,040
Yeah, well, I do want to say one thing though first,
嗯，不过我想先说一件事，

514
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:57,960
which is it seems a bit dismal if we look at the federal level
如果我们看看联邦层面，情况似乎相当糟糕

515
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,720
to answer the question.
来回答这个问题。

516
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:01,840
But things are happening right now
但眼下事情正在发生

517
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:03,480
on the state and local level.
在州和地方层面。

518
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:05,440
It seems like that's kind of all we're championing today,
看起来，我们今天所倡导的，

519
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,760
is state and local, but it is true.
是州和地方层面的，但这是事实。

520
00:26:06,760 --> 00:26:08,960
Like civics education on the state level
比如，州级的公民教育

521
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:11,640
is starting to boom in the last five years.
在过去五年里正蓬勃发展。

522
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:14,720
There's over 240 bills right now in the house
目前，国会里已经有超过240项法案

523
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:16,240
and various houses across the country
以及全国各地的各个州议会

524
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:19,560
in 40 different states changing how we do civics education.
在40个不同州，正在改变公民教育的方式。

525
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:23,080
We're really trying to bring up that rather low proficiency.
我们真的在努力提升那如此低的水平。

526
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:25,800
As to why it's been so low for so long,
至于为什么它长期以来都这么低，

527
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:28,480
there's so many reasons you can blame Sputnik.
有很多原因可以归咎于斯普特尼克。

528
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,400
You can blame the space race.
你也可以归咎于太空竞赛。

529
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,680
You can blame, what was the thing we were talking about?
你也可以归咎于我们之前提到的那个问题？

530
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:35,960
Like the change, the lack of social studies movement.
比如，变革，社会研究课程的缺失。

531
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:38,280
There are so many reasons that it has dwindled
原因太多了，它已经大幅衰退了

532
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:39,780
in the last 40 to 50 years,
在过去的40到50年里，

533
00:26:39,780 --> 00:26:42,520
but I will say on the local level, it is on the rise.
但我要说，在地方层面，它正在回升。

534
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,000
There are a ton of organizations doing a ton of work
现在有大量组织在投入大量工作

535
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:47,720
to improve civic education in the US.
致力于改善美国的公民教育。

536
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:49,480
That's why our show was kind of created.
正是这个原因，我们的节目才被构思出来。

537
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:51,280
It was conceived as civics, sorry,
它最初是作为公民教育被构想的，

538
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,080
schoolhouse rock for adults,
学校之外，面向成年人的教育，

539
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:55,880
because a lot of adults didn't get a tremendous
因为很多成年人并没有获得充分的

540
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:59,640
civics education in the 1980s or the 1990s, including me.
公民教育，包括我自己在1980年代或1990年代的经历。

541
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,080
So this is important.
所以这一点很重要。

542
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:04,560
It's important to have these outside organizations
拥有这些外部组织

543
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:06,240
trying to improve civic education.
致力于改善公民教育，

544
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:09,520
Well, you also spoke to civics teachers in an episode
嗯，你也在某期节目中采访过公民教育教师，

545
00:27:09,520 --> 00:27:12,800
and you asked them, like, give us some context here.
还问了他们，比如，给我们一些背景信息。

546
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:15,900
Why do you think there's this disconnect
你认为这种在公民教育上的脱节，

547
00:27:15,900 --> 00:27:19,260
in American society around why and how to teach civics?
在美国社会中，关于为什么要教公民课，以及如何教，究竟存在什么断层？

548
00:27:19,260 --> 00:27:21,940
But also why are we doing so poorly at it, Hannah?
但为什么我们在这件事上做得如此糟糕，汉娜？

549
00:27:21,940 --> 00:27:23,420
What did they tell you?
他们告诉了你什么？

550
00:27:23,420 --> 00:27:26,380
Teachers are experiencing an immense amount of,
教师们正承受着巨大的压力，

551
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:27,900
and this is what they have told us,
而这正是他们告诉我们的，

552
00:27:27,900 --> 00:27:31,300
restriction or the implication of restriction.
限制或限制的暗示。

553
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:34,980
I think that when it comes to divisive concepts laws,
我认为，当涉及到有争议的概念法律时，

554
00:27:34,980 --> 00:27:37,420
there might be a sense of,
可能有一种感觉是，

555
00:27:37,420 --> 00:27:39,660
we are helping teachers better understand
我们是在帮助教师更好地理解

556
00:27:39,660 --> 00:27:40,740
what they are allowed to teach.
他们被允许教授的内容。

557
00:27:40,740 --> 00:27:44,180
but a lot of teachers were not so much struggling with that.
但很多教师并没有因此感到太困扰。

558
00:27:44,180 --> 00:27:46,260
I know a lot of teachers.
我知道很多教师。

559
00:27:46,260 --> 00:27:48,500
They really want you to know that they are not
他们真的希望你知道，他们并不是

560
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:50,820
in an indoctrination project.
在灌输项目中。

561
00:27:50,820 --> 00:27:53,820
They are really in a democracy project, little d.
他们真的在搞一个民主项目，小d。

562
00:27:53,820 --> 00:27:55,860
And they want your children, they
他们想要你们的孩子，他们

563
00:27:55,860 --> 00:27:58,380
want their students to take lessons,
希望他们的学生去上课，

564
00:27:58,380 --> 00:28:01,900
but then do with it what they will, empowered to do it
但随后又得根据他们自己能做什么去处理它

565
00:28:01,900 --> 00:28:05,940
