00:28:05,940 --> 00:28:10,020
And so for these teachers who are being told what not to teach,
所以对于那些被明确告知哪些内容不能教的教师们，

567
00:28:10,020 --> 00:28:12,740
that actually makes their job much more complicated
这实际上让他们的工作变得更加复杂

568
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:15,320
because they're building curricula
因为他们正在制定课程内容

569
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:19,500
with their state and local education officials
与州和地方教育官员一起制定

570
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:21,420
and having to restrict that curricula
还要对这些课程内容进行限制

571
00:28:21,420 --> 00:28:23,780
or just worry about whether or not something
或者只是担心某些内容

572
00:28:23,780 --> 00:28:25,820
that they have been teaching for 30 years
他们过去30年一直教过的内容

573
00:28:25,820 --> 00:28:27,580
is going to be perceived
是否会被认为

574
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:29,580
as something that should not be taught anymore.
是应该被取消教学的内容。

575
00:28:29,580 --> 00:28:31,380
It's really that perception
那是一种看法

576
00:28:31,380 --> 00:28:33,500
that makes a lot of teachers afraid.
这让很多老师感到害怕。

577
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:37,300
And I think that there's some fatigue there as well.
而且我认为其中也有些疲惫。

578
00:28:37,300 --> 00:28:39,660
Every teacher we talked to is so devoted
我们每一位交谈的老师都如此投入

579
00:28:39,660 --> 00:28:43,900
But you can see it in their eyes and hear it in their voice, that they went into this
但你能在他们的眼神和语气中看到，他们投身于这一领域

580
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:51,340
field in part to actively help children and by way of that actively help community, other
部分是为了积极帮助儿童，由此也积极帮助社区和其他人

581
00:28:51,340 --> 00:28:57,980
citizens and to be told that, you know, the implication here is that you're indoctrinating
并被告诉，你知道，这里的含义是你们在灌输

582
00:28:57,980 --> 00:29:00,580
or you're teaching the wrong things.
或者你们在教错误的东西。

583
00:29:00,580 --> 00:29:04,940
That I think on an emotional level hurts, on a perception level really hurts.
我认为在情感层面是伤害性的，在认知层面更是造成了极大的伤害。

584
00:29:04,940 --> 00:29:09,900
And so it, I think Steinmeister teachers who just, they just want you to know that they
而我想到，那些中学教师，他们只是希望你们知道，

585
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:12,860
are genuinely acting in good faith.
他们确实是出于善意而行动的。

586
00:29:12,860 --> 00:29:16,260
Well, Cynthia in Salem, Virginia has this tip.
不过，萨姆特州的辛西娅就有这样一个建议。

587
00:29:16,260 --> 00:29:18,540
I was a middle school teacher who taught civics.
我曾是一名中学教师，教过公民课。

588
00:29:18,540 --> 00:29:22,660
Looking back now, I think it might be useful for teachers to give a project to their students
回过头来看，我认为老师给学生布置一个项目可能很有用。

589
00:29:22,660 --> 00:29:27,700
where they champion a certain cause and have them promote that cause by designing a campaign
让他们为某个议题发声，并通过策划一场宣传活动来推广这个议题。

590
00:29:27,700 --> 00:29:31,820
through local, state, or federal government, then present their project to the class.
通过向地方、州或联邦政府提出建议，然后将他们的项目在课堂上展示出来。

591
00:29:31,820 --> 00:29:33,640
that way kids can see the different approaches
这样孩子们就能看到基层运动中的不同做法

592
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,040
for a grassroots campaign
针对一场基层运动

593
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:36,940
and how they approach the various leaders
以及他们如何接触各种领导人

594
00:29:36,940 --> 00:29:39,680
and work with fellow citizens who join their cause.
并和共同参与他们事业的公民们合作。

595
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:41,560
Give kids the tools and the vision
给孩子们工具和愿景

596
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:45,120
to be involved as voters and active citizens.
让他们成为有参与感的选民和积极参与的公民。

597
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:46,560
We also got this question from Doug
我们还收到了Doug提出的一个问题

598
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:49,200
who says, very happy to hear civics being discussed today.
他说，非常高兴看到公民教育正在被讨论。

599
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,560
I'd like to hear how well most civics curricula
我想知道目前大多数公民教育课程

600
00:29:51,560 --> 00:29:54,480
address the temptations of autocratic, authoritarian
在应对专制、权威主义倾向方面做得如何

601
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:56,240
and populist forms of government.
以及民粹主义形式的政府。

602
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:57,080
Nick?
尼克？

603
00:29:57,080 --> 00:29:58,360
Yeah, that's a very interesting question.
嗯，这个问题非常有意思。

